# Backend deploy env vars — copy to /mnt/ssd/@docker/leetcodeview/.env on
# the VPS (see deploy.sh, which sources this path before `docker stack
# deploy -c .ci/stack.yml`).
#
# Honest current state: this file has no REQUIRED variables today — none
# of the ones below are referenced via `${VAR}` substitution in
# .ci/stack.yml, and the API has no auth/DB/external service yet that
# would need a real secret. The file still needs to EXIST on the VPS
# (even empty) — deploy.sh's `source "$ENV_PATH"` fails under `set -e` if
# the path doesn't exist at all. Treat this as a placeholder + a home for
# real secrets once there are any (e.g. once Fase 4 "Autenticação/contas"
# or a database happen — see tasks.md).
#
# Optional overrides you CAN already use, if you want to change them at
# deploy time without touching application.properties: Quarkus maps
# environment variables to config keys automatically (dots/dashes become
# underscores, all uppercase). Defaults shown are what ships today.
# RATE_LIMIT_EXECUTIONS_MAX_REQUESTS=10
# RATE_LIMIT_EXECUTIONS_WINDOW_SECONDS=60
# RATE_LIMIT_ANALYSIS_MAX_REQUESTS=30
# RATE_LIMIT_ANALYSIS_WINDOW_SECONDS=60
